==Enemy==
This enemy looks underwhelming at first due to his low stats and one knockback, but has a rapid Area Attack with double the range of [[Those Guys]] and a 15% chance to knockback Cats, becoming a hindrance to short-ranged cats like [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]]. Unless they have immunity to knockback, meatshields and tankers stand no chance against large swarms of them constantly repelling your units.

While this enemy is indeed irritating due to how he is used, his range doesn't mean much compared to things like [[Mr. Mole]] or [[Henry]]. Hence, he is not a very prominent threat in all of his appearances, excluding maybe [[Perfume Room]].

==Strategy==
Trolly Blogger's range allows him to hide behind many close-ranged attackers, such as [[Gory|Gories]], [[Otta-smack-u]], or even [[Bore]]s. Even so, he is easily defeated by cats with long-ranged Area Attacks, such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. [[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave Attackers]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] work especially well since the [[Wave Attack]]s they produce will usually kill all Trolly Bloggers in range.

Alternatively, Trolly Blogger's knockback effect and low damage can be abused by units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], as it will reset their animations and cause them to attack again. This is notable against [[Cruel Angel Clionel]] in [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]] and [[New Testament (Deadly)|New Testament]], where Maglev Cat could be used to both eliminate the Trolly Bloggers and keep Clionel pinned in the start.

